incr-update: the named update scenarios, each hop judged IN-79's four
ways (spec/harness.md "incr-update"; spec/incr.md IN-75, IN-75a, IN-78,
IN-79; H-1, WP-223).

  cargo xtask incr-update [--quick] [--only <scenario>,...] [--target a64|x64|i386,...]
                          [--compiler gcc|kiln,...] [--subject mortar|<name>|<path>]
                          [-j N] [--keep] [--self-test]

Files
  lane.py        the lane: scenarios, hops, the three links (F, G, X), the summary
  ../l10/judge.py  the ONE judge: judge_step(tools, x, f, base, new, hop=Hop)
  duty.py        IN-78's derived table as data, and the test that it agrees with the spec
  selftest.py    the judge's units (no link): dirty, stderr, elflint, (d), duty, expect
  subjects/      deliberately wrong subjects for --self-test (one per check)
  scenarios/<name>/scenario   key: value lines (below); sources beside it
  scenarios/_common/          headers every scenario may include (asm.h, print_exit.h)

A scenario
  proves: <one line: what it proves once updates exist>      (required)
  source: <where the shape comes from>                        (required)
  edit [MACRO]: <files compiled with -DMACRO in a hop that names MACRO>
  hops: -, EDIT, -, EDIT        the first link, then hop 1, 2, 3 (the default)
  link: <inputs in order>                                     (required)
  archive <name>: <unit.o | unit=name.o> ...   thin-archive <name>: <unit.o> ...
  options: <linker options>     cflags: <compiler flags after the configuration's>
  compilers: gcc [kiln]         targets: a64 x64 [i386]       not <compiler|target>: <why>
  nolibc: yes                   (no libc: `-static -m <emulation>`, entry _start)
  also-reversed: <why>          (the series again from the edited side)
  expect-full: <reason> (<detail>): <why>
                                (no hop after the first may be an update by rule: check
                                `expect`; the --gc-sections scenarios say
                                `update-not-implemented (layout)` when every hop flips a
                                section's liveness: WP-225 gc-lift, until M2b-3)

Configurations are tests/l10/build.py's `<gcc|kiln>-<a64|x64|i386>-O0-nog-nofs-static`.
By the operator's ruling (2026-11-17) AArch64 and x86-64 are required; i386
runs only with `--target i386`, with the same scenario files, and an
i386-only failure is parked.

Each hop: the inputs installed in W (a changed object as a new inode), a
directory h<i> with copies of them; F the plain full link (h<i>/f), G the
incremental-mode full link (`--incremental=full`, h<i>), X the subject
(`--incremental`, in W, MORTAR_INCR_DIRTY=h<i>/dirty.txt,
`--incremental-report=h<i>/rep.txt`). Work: <target>/incr-update/run/<label>,
removed when the run passes unless --keep.
